       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Apple Pay Prepares India Launch with Axis Bank, Faces Initial Bank Delays</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tech</span> <span>#Fintech</span> <span>#Apple</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>Apple Pay is reportedly set to launch in India today, with Axis Bank identified as a key initial partner. This move marks Apple's entry into India's rapidly expanding digital payments market, a sector that has seen significant growth and competition.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/apple-pay-prepares-india-launch-with-axis-bank-faces-initial.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>However, the rollout may not be comprehensive from the outset. Sources indicate that several of India's largest banking institutions are currently holding off on supporting Apple Pay during its initial phase. This suggests a potentially staggered adoption across the country's financial landscape.</p><p>The reasons for these initial hesitations by some major banks are not detailed in the available information. Such decisions could stem from various factors, including integration complexities, existing digital payment infrastructure, or strategic considerations regarding their own proprietary payment solutions.</p><p>Apple Pay's success in other global markets has often relied on broad bank participation to ensure widespread usability for consumers. Its introduction in India, even with limited initial bank support, could still influence the digital payments ecosystem. The service aims to offer a secure and convenient method for transactions using Apple devices.</p><p>The initial phase will likely serve as a test for Apple's strategy in a market known for its diverse payment preferences and robust local fintech players. The partnership with Axis Bank provides a foundational platform for the service's introduction.</p><p>What to watch: The timeline for broader bank adoption and Apple Pay's market penetration.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/29/apple-pay-set-to-launch-in-india-with-axis-bank-today-sources-say/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
