     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Chepauk Stadium to Honor Cricket Legends with Dedicated Stands</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#TNCA</span> <span>#Chepauk</span> <span>#Ravichandran Ashwin</span></div>
       <p>The M.A. Chidambaram Stadium, affectionately known as Chepauk, is set to immortalize three of Tamil Nadu's most celebrated cricket figures by dedicating stands in their names. The Tamil Nadu Cricket Association (TNCA) has announced plans to honor these stalwarts, recognizing their immense contributions to the sport.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/chepauk-stadium-to-honor-cricket-legends-with-dedicated-stan.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This move will see stands at the iconic Chennai venue named after Ravichandran Ashwin, Kris Srikkanth, and S. Venkataraghavan. Each of these cricketers has left an indelible mark on Indian and international cricket, bringing glory and recognition to their home state.</p><p>Ravichandran Ashwin, a contemporary spin wizard, continues to be a pivotal player for India in Test cricket, known for his guile and record-breaking performances. His career has seen him become one of the most successful bowlers in the history of the game.</p><p>Kris Srikkanth, a flamboyant opening batsman, captivated fans with his aggressive style during the 1980s and early 90s. He was a key member of India's 1983 World Cup-winning squad and later served as a national selector.</p><p>S. Venkataraghavan, a classical off-spinner, was part of India's famous spin quartet of the 1970s. He also captained India and had a distinguished career as an international umpire, further cementing his legacy in cricket.</p><p>The dedication of these stands will serve as a permanent tribute to their achievements and inspire future generations of cricketers from Tamil Nadu. It's a fitting recognition at a stadium that has witnessed many of their memorable performances.</p><p>What to watch: The official ceremony unveiling the newly named stands at Chepauk.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary regarding the naming of stands at Chepauk.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/tnca-to-name-three-stands-at-chepauk-after-ashwin-srikkanth-and-venkataraghavan-7409/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
