       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Congress Working Committee Meet: Key Demands On CEC Resignation And Voter Roll Row</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#Congress</span> <span>#CEC</span></div>
       <p>The Congress Working Committee (CWC) recently convened, addressing several critical issues that have drawn national attention. The meeting focused on key demands, particularly concerning the resignation of the Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) and allegations surrounding a voter roll row.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/congress-working-committee-meet-key-demands-on-cec-resignati.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the CWC meet, prominent discussions revolved around the call for the CEC's resignation. This demand signifies a serious concern raised by the party regarding the conduct or impartiality perceived within the electoral body's leadership. The specifics of the allegations leading to this demand were central to the committee's deliberations.</p><p>Additionally, the CWC addressed a significant controversy involving the voter rolls. This &quot;voter roll row&quot; implies concerns over the accuracy, integrity, or fairness of the electoral lists. Such issues can have profound implications for democratic processes, potentially affecting voter eligibility and election outcomes.</p><p>The committee's focus on these two points underscores their perceived importance in the current political climate. The Congress party appears to be emphasizing electoral transparency and accountability as core issues, pushing for reforms or investigations into the alleged irregularities.</p><p>What to watch: Official responses from the Election Commission regarding these demands.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly captures the essence of the headlines provided in the source summary.</p>
