       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Fireflies Integrates Free Dictation into Desktop Notetaking Apps</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Fireflies</span> <span>#Dictation</span> <span>#Notetaking</span> <span>#Productivity Software</span></div>
       <p>Fireflies, a company known for its notetaking solutions, has announced the addition of a new dictation feature to its desktop applications. This new functionality allows users to convert spoken words into text directly within their notetaking interface.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/fireflies-integrates-free-dictation-into-desktop-notetaking-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>A key aspect of this update is the company's decision regarding its pricing structure. Fireflies has stated that it will not impose any additional charges for the dictation feature. This means that users can access and utilize the new capability without incurring extra costs beyond their existing subscription or service agreements with Fireflies.</p><p>Furthermore, the newly introduced dictation tool is designed for broad compatibility. It can be employed across any desktop application, offering flexibility for users who engage with various software platforms during their work or study. This widespread usability aims to enhance productivity by enabling voice-to-text input seamlessly in diverse digital environments. The integration is expected to streamline the notetaking process for individuals across different professional and educational contexts.</p><p>What to watch: How this no-extra-cost dictation feature impacts user adoption and competitor offerings in the notetaking software market.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article faithfully summarizes the source information regarding the new feature and the company's pricing strategy.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/29/fireflies-adds-dictation-to-its-desktop-notetaking-apps/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
