       <h1>India Beat Qatar 3-2 To Enter Quarter-Finals Of Men's Volleyball In Asian Games</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Volleyball</span> <span>#AsianGames</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>The Indian men’s volleyball team secured a narrow 3‑2 victory over Qatar on Tuesday, extending its winning streak and clinching a third successive triumph in the Asian Games campaign. The win propelled India into the quarter‑finals, confirming its place among the tournament’s top contenders. The five‑set contest showcased a tightly contested battle, with both sides exchanging points before India edged ahead in the decisive set. The result marked the team’s third victory of the group stage, reinforcing its momentum heading into the knockout rounds. Coaches praised the players’ resilience and tactical adjustments that proved decisive in the closing stages. The quarter‑final placement also adds to India’s growing profile in Asian volleyball, where the squad has been steadily improving its international standing. Fans and analysts will now turn their attention to the upcoming knockout fixtures, where India will aim to build on the confidence generated by the Qatar win. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/india-beat-qatar-3-2-to-enter-quarter-finals-of-mens-volleyb.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: India’s quarter‑final opponent and the team’s ability to sustain its winning form under pressure.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly summarizes the match result and tournament progression.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/volleyball/india-beat-qatar-3-2-to-enter-quarter-finals-of-mens-volleyball-in-asian-games-12114208#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
