  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/sports">sports</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India to Face Sri Lanka in Asian Games Cricket Semi-Final After Quarter-Final Abandonment</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Sri Lanka</span></div>
       <p>India is poised to meet Sri Lanka in the men's cricket semi-final at the Asian Games 2026, following an unexpected turn of events in the quarter-final stage. The highly anticipated match-up was confirmed after Sri Lanka's quarter-final encounter against Nepal was abandoned without a single ball being bowled. This abandonment occurred on Tuesday in Nisshin, Japan, as reported by Cricinfo, due to circumstances that prevented play.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/india-to-face-sri-lanka-in-asian-games-cricket-semi-final-af.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The decision to abandon the match meant that Sri Lanka advanced to the semi-finals, setting the stage for a compelling contest against the Indian squad. The Asian Games cricket tournament has been a focal point for national pride and sporting excellence, with teams vying for coveted medals. India enters the semi-final as a formidable opponent, aiming to secure its spot in the final, while Sri Lanka will be looking to leverage their progression despite the rain-affected quarter-final. The unpredictable nature of weather in outdoor sports often plays a crucial role, and this instance has significantly shaped the tournament's knockout phase.</p><p>What to watch: The high-stakes semi-final between India and Sri Lanka.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly conveys the information provided in the summary regarding the Asian Games cricket match.</p>
