       <h1>India Women Eye Asian Games Hockey Final Spot Against South Korea</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Hockey</span> <span>#India Women</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#Semifinal</span></div>
       <p>The Indian women's hockey team is set to compete in a crucial semifinal clash against South Korea, aiming for a spot in the Asian Games final. The match, scheduled for Wednesday, will take place at the Kawasaki Juko Stadium, marking a significant moment in their campaign.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/india-women-eye-asian-games-hockey-final-spot-against-south-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India enters the semifinal stage with an impressive unbeaten record throughout the competition. This consistent performance has fueled aspirations of securing a long-awaited gold medal at the Asian Games. The team is looking to end a 44-year drought for top honours in the event.</p><p>Their opponent, South Korea, stands between them and the final. The semifinal encounter is expected to be a challenging contest, with both teams vying for a chance to play for the gold. The Indian contingent will rely on their strong form and tactical discipline demonstrated in previous matches.</p><p>Achieving success in this semifinal would not only propel them into the final but also bring them one step closer to making history by clinching the coveted gold medal. The focus will be on maintaining their unbeaten streak and executing their game plan effectively against a formidable South Korean side.</p><p>What to watch: India's strategy against South Korea in the semifinal.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft provides a faithful summary of the source, maintaining the context of the upcoming semifinal.</p>
