     <article class="story single" data-beat="environment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Mongabay India · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India's Coking Coal Ambitions Highlight Methane Emission Concerns</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Environment</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Coal Mining</span> <span>#Methane Emissions</span></div>
       <p>India is embarking on an ambitious plan to significantly increase its coking coal production, with a strategic goal to double output by 2030. This substantial expansion is primarily aimed at meeting the escalating demands of the nation's burgeoning steel manufacturing sector, a crucial industry for economic development. While the environmental impact of carbon emissions from the combustion of coal is a well-understood and frequently discussed topic, the process of coal mining itself presents another significant environmental challenge: the release of methane emissions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/indias-coking-coal-ambitions-highlight-methane-emission-conc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Methane is a powerful greenhouse gas, and its presence in the atmosphere contributes to climate change. The emissions generated during coal extraction necessitate early and proactive attention from policymakers and industry stakeholders. Experts underscore the critical importance of integrating comprehensive monitoring and effective abatement measures right from the initial planning stages of this coking coal expansion. Neglecting to incorporate these vital environmental safeguards at the outset risks &quot;locking in&quot; higher levels of methane emissions for years to come. Such an oversight could complicate future efforts to mitigate environmental impacts, despite the economic imperative driving the increased coal output. Therefore, a balanced approach that addresses both economic growth and environmental stewardship, particularly concerning methane, is essential for India's industrial future.</p><p>What to watch: The development of national strategies to integrate methane emission controls into new coal mining projects.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source material without adding external claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://india.mongabay.com/2026/09/indias-coking-coal-push-needs-a-methane-plan-commentary/" rel="noopener">Mongabay India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
