     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jadeja or Axar? India to make 'utility' decision ahead of 2027 World Cup</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#World Cup</span> <span>#Selection</span></div>
       <p>The Indian cricket team faces a significant selection conundrum concerning its spin-bowling all-rounders as preparations for the 2027 World Cup begin to take shape. The central debate revolves around the contrasting yet equally valuable utility of Ravindra Jadeja and Axar Patel, a decision that could profoundly impact the team's balance and strategic approach.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/jadeja-or-axar-india-to-make-utility-decision-ahead-of-2027-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>According to spin coach Sairaj Bahutule, the team management is not rushing into a definitive choice. Bahutule indicated that a final call on who will be the preferred option will be made after India's upcoming series. This suggests a period of evaluation, allowing both players to showcase their form and adaptability in varied match scenarios.</p><p>Crucially, the decision will also be heavily influenced by the conditions expected at the 2027 World Cup venues. This pragmatic approach underscores the team's commitment to tailoring its squad to specific environmental challenges, ensuring maximum effectiveness on the global stage. The tactical nuances of pitch characteristics, boundary sizes, and opposition strengths will all play a part in determining which spin all-rounder provides the optimal balance.</p><p>What to watch: The performance of both spinners in the upcoming series will be key.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source information regarding the selection process for spin-bowling all-rounders.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1556124.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
