       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Leaks Suggest Minimal Design Changes for Google's Upcoming Pixel 11A</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Google</span> <span>#Pixel 11A</span> <span>#Smartphone</span> <span>#Leaks</span></div>
       <p>Google appears poised to introduce its next midrange smartphone, the Pixel 11A, with minimal design overhauls. According to recent leaks initially reported by Android Headlines, the device is not expected to diverge significantly in appearance from its current lineup.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/leaks-suggest-minimal-design-changes-for-googles-upcoming-pi.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Image renders, attributed to OnLeaks, provide what is potentially the first public glimpse of the Pixel 11A. These visuals suggest a design ethos that closely mirrors its predecessors, specifically appearing almost indistinguishable from the Pixel 10A. The most notable, albeit subtle, change identified is a slightly rounder, oval-shaped rear camera module.</p><p>This continuity in design indicates that Google may be focusing its development efforts elsewhere, perhaps on internal hardware upgrades, software optimizations, or maintaining a specific cost structure for its A-series. The Pixel A-series has historically aimed to offer a more budget-friendly entry point into the Pixel ecosystem, retaining core features while managing price.</p><p>The absence of major aesthetic changes could also streamline production and supply chain processes. While these renders offer an early look, official details concerning the Pixel 11A's full specifications, features, and release schedule are still pending from Google. The consistent design language suggests an evolutionary rather than revolutionary update for the device's external appearance.</p><p>What to watch: Official announcements from Google detailing the internal specifications and software enhancements of the Pixel 11A.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Clean adaptation of the provided leak details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1002072/google-pixel-11a-leaked-renders-first-look" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
