     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>LPU Violence: SIT Formed, CCTV Footage Under Scanner; Punjab Police Warn Of Strict Action</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#LPU Violence</span> <span>#Punjab Police</span> <span>#SIT</span> <span>#CCTV</span></div>
       <p>A Special Investigation Team (SIT) has been established to investigate the recent violence that occurred at Lovely Professional University (LPU). The authorities have initiated a thorough review of available CCTV footage, which is currently under scanner as a crucial part of the ongoing probe. This step aims to identify individuals involved and gather critical evidence related to the incidents.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/lpu-violence-sit-formed-cctv-footage-under-scanner-punjab-po.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Punjab Director General of Police (DGP) Gaurav Yadav made a visit to the LPU campus on Monday. Following his assessment of the situation, DGP Yadav issued a clear warning, stating that stringent action would be pursued against anyone found to be complicit in the acts of violence. This statement underscores the commitment of the Punjab Police to maintain law and order and ensure accountability.</p><p>The formation of the SIT signifies a focused approach to unravelling the circumstances surrounding the disturbances. Officials are leveraging technological resources, such as CCTV footage analysis, to piece together the sequence of events and identify culprits. The police's firm stance indicates a determination to deter future incidents and uphold peace within educational institutions. The investigation is anticipated to proceed diligently, with all evidence being meticulously examined to bring those responsible to justice.</p><p>What to watch: The progress of the SIT investigation and any subsequent actions taken by the Punjab Police.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary without adding unverified claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
