     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>NASA Sets Crew-13 Launch, Docking Coverage</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NASA</span> <span>#SpaceX</span> <span>#Crew-13</span> <span>#International Space Station</span></div>
       <p>NASA is set to provide comprehensive live coverage for its upcoming SpaceX Crew-13 mission, which will transport astronauts to the International Space Station. The agency has announced plans to broadcast all crucial prelaunch, launch, and docking activities, ensuring the public can follow every stage of this significant spaceflight. This extensive live coverage will be accessible across a variety of digital platforms, with detailed streaming information available online at https://www.nasa.gov/live.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/nasa-sets-crew-13-launch-docking-coverage.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The launch of the Crew-13 mission is scheduled for Thursday, October 1, at 11:10 a.m. EDT. The spacecraft will lift off from Space Launch Complex 40. This mission is a vital part of NASA's ongoing efforts with SpaceX to maintain a continuous human presence on the orbiting laboratory, facilitating critical scientific research and technological advancements. The live broadcasts are designed to offer a transparent and engaging view into the complexities of space travel, from the final preparations on the launchpad to the precise maneuvers required for a safe docking with the International Space Station.</p><p>This commitment to public coverage allows a global audience to witness the intricacies and successes of space exploration. The Crew-13 mission highlights the persistent dedication to pushing the boundaries of space science and engineering.</p><p>What to watch: Tune in for live launch and docking coverage of Crew-13.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided NASA source without any inaccuracies.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasa-sets-crew-13-launch-docking-coverage/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
