     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ranbir Kapoor starrer Love &amp;#038; War poster gets a road safety twist from Mumbai Police; ‘LoveAndSafetyOnRoad’ message goes viral</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Mumbai Police</span> <span>#Road Safety</span></div>
       <p>Sanjay Leela Bhansali’s highly anticipated upcoming film, &quot;Love &amp; War,&quot; starring Ranbir Kapoor, has become an unexpected part of a public awareness campaign. The Mumbai Police have ingeniously repurposed the film's first-look poster to promote road safety, specifically emphasizing the critical importance of wearing a seat belt while driving.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/ranbir-kapoor-starrer-love-038-war-poster-gets-a-road-safety.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This creative adaptation by the Mumbai Police has given the film's promotional material a unique and impactful twist. By integrating a vital safety message with a popular cultural reference, the campaign aims to capture public attention more effectively. The initiative has quickly gained traction, with the message &quot;LoveAndSafetyOnRoad&quot; reportedly going viral across various platforms.</p><p>The use of a prominent film poster featuring a major star like Ranbir Kapoor demonstrates an innovative approach to public service announcements. It leverages the widespread appeal and visibility of Bollywood cinema to disseminate crucial information about road safety. This collaboration, albeit indirect, highlights how popular entertainment can be utilized for significant social causes, reaching a broad audience with essential advice. The campaign has succeeded in generating buzz not only for road safety but also for the upcoming film itself.</p><p>What to watch: If more such creative collaborations between public services and entertainment emerge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the Bollywood Hungama report on the Mumbai Police campaign.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ranbir-kapoor-starrer-love-loveandsafetyonroad-message-goes-viral/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
