     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Silent Aortic Disease Can Offer a Narrow Window to Save the Heart’s Own Valve</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#aortic disease</span> <span>#aneurysm</span> <span>#heart health</span> <span>#David Procedure</span></div>
       <p>Aortic root aneurysms, a serious heart condition, often progress silently, making early detection a significant challenge. This &quot;silent&quot; nature means the disease can advance substantially before symptoms manifest, narrowing the window for effective intervention. On World Heart Day, Dr. Varun Shetty, a Senior Consultant in Adult Cardiac Surgery and Paediatric and Congenital Heart Surgery at Narayana Health City, emphasized the critical importance of early referral.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/silent-aortic-disease-can-offer-a-narrow-window-to-save-the-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Dr. Shetty highlighted that timely referral can be pivotal for patients considering valve-sparing surgery. He discussed the David Procedure, a specific surgical technique designed to preserve the heart's own aortic valve while repairing the aneurysm. Understanding such procedures and their benefits is vital for patients and their families.</p><p>Despite advancements, long-term follow-up for patients with aortic disease remains a significant challenge in India. Ensuring consistent monitoring after surgery is crucial for optimal outcomes and detecting any potential complications. The discussion underscores the need for increased awareness, improved diagnostic pathways, and robust post-operative care infrastructure to address this complex cardiac condition effectively.</p><p>What to watch: Efforts to improve early diagnosis and long-term patient follow-up for aortic conditions in India.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the expert's points regarding aortic root aneurysms and the David Procedure.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/silent-aortic-disease-can-offer-a-narrow-window-to-save-the-hearts-own-valve/134557292" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
