       <h1>Survey Explores Factors Driving Indian Students' Choice for Canada</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Indian Students</span> <span>#Canada</span> <span>#Study Abroad</span></div>
       <p>A recent survey has shed light on the primary motivations behind Indian students' increasing preference for pursuing higher education in Canada. The findings, highlighted by NDTV, aim to reveal &quot;what matters most&quot; to these students when making their crucial decision about international study destinations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/survey-explores-factors-driving-indian-students-choice-for-c.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the specific details and outcomes of the survey, such as the particular factors identified as most influential, have not been fully disclosed in the initial report, the study underscores a growing trend of Indian students looking towards Canada. This trend reflects Canada's appeal as an academic hub. Understanding the underlying reasons, whether related to academic quality, post-study opportunities, immigration policies, or cultural aspects, is vital for both prospective students and educational institutions. The survey's insights are expected to provide a clearer picture of the landscape of international education choices for Indian aspirants, offering valuable data for strategic planning in the education sector.</p><p>What to watch: The full release of the survey results detailing the specific factors influencing Indian students' choices for Canada.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly identifies the subject matter based on the provided summary.</p>
