     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Three Gujarat Men Kidnapped in Ethiopia, Rs 1 Crore Ransom Demanded</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National News</span> <span>#Crime</span> <span>#International Incident</span> <span>#Gujarat</span></div>
       <p>Three individuals from Gujarat, who were reportedly on a journey bound for the United States, have been kidnapped while in Ethiopia. Their respective families in India have subsequently received a ransom demand totaling Rs 1 crore for their safe return.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/three-gujarat-men-kidnapped-in-ethiopia-rs-1-crore-ransom-de.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The abduction has plunged the families into a state of profound distress, as they navigate the sudden and severe international incident. While the precise details surrounding the kidnapping, such as the specific location within Ethiopia and the identity of those responsible, are not fully elaborated in the available information, the gravity of the situation is clear.</p><p>The men's intended passage to the US has been abruptly halted by this criminal act. Such incidents of kidnapping for ransom, particularly those involving individuals traveling internationally, often present complex diplomatic and logistical challenges for both government authorities and the affected families.</p><p>The substantial ransom demand of Rs 1 crore underscores the serious nature of the abduction and places an immediate and significant financial burden on the families. While specific information on ongoing efforts to secure the release of the three men and address the ransom is not publicly detailed, the situation requires urgent attention.</p><p>This event serves as a stark reminder of the inherent risks that can be encountered by individuals undertaking international travel, particularly those on migratory paths, and highlights potential vulnerabilities in various regions.</p><p>What to watch: Updates on the safety of the kidnapped men and efforts to facilitate their release.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides an accurate summary of the kidnapping incident as described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/gujarat/story/us-bound-3-gujarat-relatives-kidnapped-in-ethiopia-family-receives-rs-1-crore-ransom-demand-3006134-2026-09-30?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
