       <p>Today News Headlines for School Assembly on September 29, 2026, as reported by The Indian Express, highlighted several key national developments. For students and faculty, awareness of current events remains crucial for a comprehensive understanding of the world. On the diplomatic front, India has sent a senior official from the Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) to Pakistan. This diplomatic engagement underscores ongoing efforts in international relations, a vital area of study for aspiring civil servants and international affairs professionals.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/today-news-headlines-for-school-assembly-september-29-2026.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Domestically, the Supreme Court has refused to impose a stay on the Merchant Discount Rate (MDR) for UPI payments. This ruling pertains to the financial sector and digital transactions, impacting how businesses and consumers interact with the Unified Payments Interface. While the summary for the school assembly did not detail specific eligibility requirements for educational programs or provide official links related to these news items, these headlines offer valuable insights into India's political and economic landscape. For those interested in careers in diplomacy, law, or finance, understanding such daily developments is foundational.</p><p>What to watch: Ongoing national and international policy discussions.</p>
