     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-09-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Trump Claims Iran War Will Conclude &quot;Very Soon&quot; and Assesses Iran as &quot;Failing Badly&quot;</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Trump</span> <span>#Iran</span> <span>#Foreign Policy</span> <span>#Nuclear Weapons</span></div>
       <p>Former President Trump recently made public statements indicating that the conflict involving Iran is anticipated to conclude &quot;very soon.&quot; He described this potential resolution as &quot;one of the most important things we did,&quot; a comment reported by News18 World.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/trump-claims-iran-war-will-conclude-very-soon-and-assesses-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In his remarks, Trump asserted that Iran was currently &quot;failing very badly.&quot; He further reiterated a consistent claim from his past, emphasizing that Tehran would not be allowed to develop or possess a nuclear weapon. These statements align with his previous public positions on Iran's regional activities and its nuclear program.</p><p>The former president's comments did not provide specific details regarding the nature of the &quot;Iran war&quot; he referenced, nor did they outline the particular mechanisms, timelines, or conditions under which such a conflict would reach a swift conclusion. His remarks underscore a continued focus on Iran's strategic posture and its potential nuclear capabilities.</p><p>Trump's repeated assertion about preventing Iran from acquiring nuclear weapons reflects a longstanding and central theme in his foreign policy discourse. The statements were made without additional context on specific diplomatic initiatives, military strategies, or intelligence assessments that might contribute to the projected rapid resolution of the situation.</p><p>What to watch: Any subsequent statements from Trump or related officials that might offer further clarification or specific details regarding these claims.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate to the text provided, adding standard framing.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/one-of-the-most-important-things-we-did-trump-says-iran-war-will-end-very-soon-ws-rt-10359908.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
