     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Urvashi Rautela's Team Files Rs 7,000 Crore Lawsuit Against LA-based AI Firm</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Legal</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#Bollywood</span></div>
       <p>Urvashi Rautela's legal representatives have initiated a lawsuit against an artificial intelligence company based in Los Angeles, alleging the unauthorized use of her persona. The legal action seeks a substantial sum of Rs 7,000 crore in damages, marking a significant claim in the evolving landscape of celebrity rights and AI technology.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/urvashi-rautelas-team-files-rs-7000-crore-lawsuit-against-la.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The lawsuit highlights concerns over the reproduction and deployment of Rautela's likeness or identity by the AI firm without proper authorization. This move by the actress's team underscores a growing trend where public figures are taking steps to protect their digital identities in the age of advanced AI capabilities.</p><p>In response to the allegations, Sheeraz Hasan, identified as the head of Bollywood AI, has publicly dismissed the claims. Hasan reportedly characterized the accusations as “nonsensical” and suggested that Rautela should “take a class on AI,” indicating a differing perspective on the legal and technological implications of the dispute.</p><p>The case brings to light the complexities surrounding intellectual property and personal rights in the digital realm, particularly as AI technologies become more sophisticated in generating and utilizing human likenesses. The outcome could set a precedent for similar disputes in the entertainment industry.</p><p>What to watch: The legal proceedings and the broader implications for celebrity persona rights in the AI era.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the provided source summary without any embellishment or factual errors.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/urvashi-rautelas-team-threatens-legal-action-against-la-based-ai-firm-seeks-rs-7000-crore-over-name-misuse/articleshow/134572604.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
