     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Variety’s ‘Pixels and Pencils’ Panel Returns to SCAD Savannah Film Festival</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Animation</span> <span>#Film Festival</span> <span>#Variety</span> <span>#SCAD</span></div>
       <p>Variety’s “Pixels and Pencils” animation panel is set to make its return to the SCAD Savannah Film Festival. This year marks the fifth consecutive year that the event has hosted this prominent discussion, solidifying its role as a key gathering point for industry professionals and enthusiasts of animated cinema.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/varietys-pixels-and-pencils-panel-returns-to-scad-savannah-f.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The panel focuses on spotlighting the directors behind the year’s most standout animated features. This year’s conversation features six filmmakers who have made significant contributions to the medium. The lineup includes Brad Bird, known for his work on Netflix’s “Ray Gunn.” Also participating is Daniel Chong, representing Pixar’s “Hoppers.”</p><p>Additionally, Joel Crawford and Januel Mercado will join the discussion, representing DreamWorks Animation’s “Forgotten Island.” The inclusion of these directors highlights the diversity of studios and styles currently shaping the animation landscape. The event provides a platform for these creators to share insights into their processes and the challenges they face in bringing their visions to life.</p><p>The presence of such a high-profile roster underscores the growing importance of animated features in the broader film industry. As animation continues to evolve, these panels serve as a crucial space for dialogue between creators, critics, and the public.</p><p>The event is expected to draw significant attention from industry insiders and fans alike, offering a glimpse into the future of animation through the perspectives of its current leaders.</p><p>What to watch: The specific insights shared by the directors regarding their latest projects and the future of animation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source information regarding the festival and the list of directors.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/film/awards/variety-pixels-and-pencils-2026-scad-animated-directors-1236878302/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
