     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>What is Virat Kohli's record at Guwahati in ODIs?</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#ViratKohli</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#Guwahati</span></div>
       <p>Virat Kohli has etched a remarkable statistical footprint at Barsapara Cricket Stadium in Guwahati. The Indian batting maestro has recorded two centuries at the venue, accumulating a total of 253 runs across his two One Day International innings. This performance translates to an impressive average of 126.50, underscoring his consistency on the Guwahati pitch. Both centuries were achieved against competitive opposition, reinforcing Kohli’s reputation as a prolific run‑maker in limited‑overs cricket. The dual centuries also highlight his ability to adapt to the conditions at Barsapara, which has become a notable ground in his ODI itinerary. While the sample size is limited to two matches, the statistical output places Kohli among the elite players with the highest averages at a single venue in the format. Cricket analysts will likely reference these figures when discussing his form ahead of future series that include matches at Guwahati. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/what-is-virat-kohlis-record-at-guwahati-in-odis.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: Whether Kohli can extend his stellar Guwahati record in upcoming ODIs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source data regarding Kohli's performance at the venue.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
