       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · Engadget · 2026-09-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Xbox just unveiled Mythic Achievements, which are basically PlayStation platinum trophies</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Xbox</span> <span>#Gaming</span> <span>#Achievements</span> <span>#Microsoft</span></div>
       <p>Xbox has officially unveiled a new addition to its player recognition system: Mythic Achievements. This new category of achievement is designed to signify a player's ultimate dedication and complete mastery of a game, acting as a clear public declaration that a title has been fully finished. The introduction of Mythic Achievements offers a new way for gamers to showcase their in-depth commitment to their favorite interactive experiences.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-29/xbox-just-unveiled-mythic-achievements-which-are-basically-p.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>These achievements are intended to provide a definitive mark of completion. Unlike standard achievements that might cover various milestones, Mythic Achievements specifically denote that all challenges, objectives, and content within a game have been thoroughly addressed. This gives players a distinct badge of honor to display their comprehensive engagement with a particular title.</p><p>A notable feature of this rollout is its retroactive application. Players who have already invested significant time and effort into completing games will find these new Mythic Achievements automatically unlocked for their past accomplishments. This means that gamers will not need to replay previously finished titles to earn these new accolades, ensuring immediate recognition for their historical achievements.</p><p>The new system enhances the existing framework, providing a deeper layer of acknowledgment for the most dedicated players. It allows the gaming community to instantly identify those who have truly &quot;beaten&quot; a game in its entirety, adding a new dimension to player profiles and competitive bragging rights.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of Mythic Achievements on player engagement and completion rates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly interprets the source summary regarding the function and retroactive nature of the new achievement system.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.engadget.com/2272478/xbox-mythic-achievements-are-here/" rel="noopener">Engadget</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
